<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Sept capacity utilisation rises to 84.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Dutch Sept capacity utilisation rises to 84.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch manufacturing capacity utilisation rose to 84.5 percent in September from 84.3 percent in June, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.</p>
<p>DUTCH MANUFACTURING CAPACITY UTILISATION</p>
<p>					    Sept 96   June 96    Sept 95</p>
<p> Total industry			  84.5	 84.3	 84.3</p>
<p> - semi-manufactured goods	   83.8	 84.1	 82.8</p>
<p> - capital goods			 85.8	 84.1	 85.8</p>
<p> - consumer goods			84.3	 84.6	 85.1</p>
<p>Note - The CBS publishes capacity utilisation data once every</p>
<p>three months.</p>
<p>Capacity utilisation figures for June 1996 have been amended as a result of revised weightings, the CBS said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
